{"The implementation relies on `queue.ShutDown` and `Queue.shutdown()`, which are not available in many Python versions. If the runtime does not support these APIs, workers will never exit cleanly and shutdown will raise at runtime. Consider using an explicit sentinel item (or a custom queue wrapper) for shutdown signaling instead of `queue` module shutdown features.": 0.6585884094238281, "`OffsetTracker.get_committable_offsets` iterates from `start` to `max_offset` and checks membership in sets, which can become expensive if offsets are sparse, if there are large gaps, or if a partition accumulates many outstanding offsets. This could introduce CPU overhead in the commit loop and delay commits.": 0.4761236011981964, "The Kafka integration test drives `StreamProcessor` via private methods (`_run_once`, `_shutdown`) and depends on timing loops/sleeps. This can be brittle and flaky across environments. Consider using public APIs (if available) and more deterministic synchronization/assertions to reduce flake risk.": 0.4556470513343811}